cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this knowledge base or software, cite it with these metadata."
title: "cnl-ckc: Controlled Natural Language Clinical Knowledge Compiler"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Turkes
    given-names: Emir
repository-code: "https://github.com/eturkes/cnl-ckc"
license-url: "https://github.com/eturkes/cnl-ckc/blob/main/LICENSE"
abstract: >-
  cnl-ckc compiles published clinical guidelines into an executable Prolog
  knowledge base through Attempto Controlled English that clinicians review
  beside each source passage. The compiled output is certified against a
  formal specification under a machine-verified kernel. The first knowledge
  base covers the CDC Clinical Practice Guideline for Prescribing Opioids for
  Pain (2022).
keywords:
  - clinical guidelines
  - controlled natural language
  - Attempto Controlled English
  - Prolog
  - knowledge base
  - formal verification
